          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A low hum grows as the sky darkens and fades toward dawn; it softens while the Moon is up. A sharp tap is moonrise or moonset. A slow swell is the Milky Way's core rising.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A low hum grows as the sky darkens and fades toward dawn; it softens while the Moon is up. A sharp tap is moonrise or moonset. A slow swell is the Milky Way's core rising."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Una vibración grave crece al oscurecer el cielo y se desvanece hacia el amanecer; se suaviza mientras la Luna está arriba. Un toque seco es la salida o la puesta de la Luna. Una ola lenta es la salida del núcleo de la Vía Láctea."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A new moon is a few sharp, sparse taps. As it fills, the taps soften over a broad hum, until a full moon is one wide swell. A waxing Moon swells across the pattern; a waning one fades. Each night's tick on the river is firmer and crisper as its score rises.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A new moon is a few sharp, sparse taps. As it fills, the taps soften over a broad hum, until a full moon is one wide swell. A waxing Moon swells across the pattern; a waning one fades. Each night's tick on the river is firmer and crisper as its score rises."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Una luna nueva son unos pocos toques nítidos y espaciados. A medida que se llena, los toques se suavizan sobre un zumbido amplio, hasta que la luna llena es una sola ola ancha. Una Luna creciente se intensifica a lo largo del patrón; una menguante se desvanece. El toque de cada noche en el río es más firme y nítido a medida que sube su índice."
          }
        }
      }
    },
