    "Aerosol optical depth at 550 nm, from the CAMS global forecast (Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service) through Open-Meteo's air-quality service, covers about five days. It is averaged over the dark window: below 0.1 is clear air, 0.1 to 0.25 light haze, 0.25 to 0.5 haze or smoke that makes the Milky Way look faint, and 0.5 or more heavy smoke or haze that hides faint stars. From 0.25 a caveat appears beside the score, and smoke caps it: at most 74 from 0.25, at most 59 from 0.5. When no smoke forecast reaches a night, nothing is capped. Air-quality data: Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service (CAMS) through Open-Meteo, CC BY 4.0, averaged over the night's true darkness by Nyx. Neither the European Commission nor ECMWF is responsible for any use that may be made of the Copernicus information or data it contains. You can switch this request off in Your privacy.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Aerosol optical depth at 550 nm, from the CAMS global forecast (Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service) through Open-Meteo's air-quality service, covers about five days. It is averaged over the dark window: below 0.1 is clear air, 0.1 to 0.25 light haze, 0.25 to 0.5 haze or smoke that makes the Milky Way look faint, and 0.5 or more heavy smoke or haze that hides faint stars. From 0.25 a caveat appears beside the score, and smoke caps it: at most 74 from 0.25, at most 59 from 0.5. When no smoke forecast reaches a night, nothing is capped. Air-quality data: Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service (CAMS) through Open-Meteo, CC BY 4.0, averaged over the night's true darkness by Nyx. Neither the European Commission nor ECMWF is responsible for any use that may be made of the Copernicus information or data it contains. You can switch this request off in Your privacy."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "La profundidad óptica de aerosoles a 550 nm, del pronóstico global CAMS (Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service) a través del servicio de calidad del aire de Open-Meteo, cubre unos cinco días. Se promedia sobre el periodo de oscuridad: menos de 0.1 es aire limpio; de 0.1 a 0.25, bruma ligera; de 0.25 a 0.5, bruma o humo que hacen ver tenue la Vía Láctea, y 0.5 o más, humo o bruma densos que ocultan las estrellas débiles. A partir de 0.25 aparece una advertencia junto al índice, y el humo lo limita: como máximo 74 desde 0.25 y como máximo 59 desde 0.5. Cuando ningún pronóstico de humo llega a una noche, no se limita nada. Datos de calidad del aire: Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service (CAMS) a través de Open-Meteo, CC BY 4.0, promediados por Nyx sobre la oscuridad total de la noche. Ni la Comisión Europea ni el ECMWF son responsables del uso que pueda hacerse de la información o los datos de Copernicus que contiene. Puedes desactivar esta solicitud en Tu privacidad."
          }
        }
      }
    },
