    "Eyes adapt to the dark in two steps. Cones settle in about 10 minutes; rods, which see faint stars and the Milky Way, need 20 to 30. Dim red light barely touches rods, and a moment of white light starts them over. This clock counts your time in field mode, so it is only an estimate.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Eyes adapt to the dark in two steps. Cones settle in about 10 minutes; rods, which see faint stars and the Milky Way, need 20 to 30. Dim red light barely touches rods, and a moment of white light starts them over. This clock counts your time in field mode, so it is only an estimate."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Los ojos se adaptan a la oscuridad en dos etapas. Los conos se ajustan en unos 10 minutos; los bastones, que ven las estrellas débiles y la Vía Láctea, necesitan de 20 a 30. La luz roja tenue apenas afecta a los bastones, y un instante de luz blanca los hace empezar de nuevo. Este reloj cuenta tu tiempo en modo de campo, así que es solo una estimación."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Eyes adjusting": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Eyes adjusting"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ojos adaptándose"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Eyes take 20 to 30 minutes to adapt to the dark. A bright screen or a white light resets them.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Eyes take 20 to 30 minutes to adapt to the dark. A bright screen or a white light resets them."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Los ojos tardan de 20 a 30 minutos en adaptarse a la oscuridad. Una pantalla brillante o una luz blanca los reinicia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
