    "Solar timing uses NOAA approximations. Moonrise and moonset use a low-precision Meeus-style position. Checked against the U.S. Naval Observatory, they agree to within a few minutes: a minute or less at the parks checked in Alaska, Hawaiʻi, American Samoa and the Virgin Islands, and under 4 minutes at mid-latitude parks. Sunrise, sunset and twilight agree to within a minute. Moon illumination corrects the mean 29.53-day cycle with the Moon's calculated position and is approximate. Terrain and atmospheric conditions can shift visible rise and set times. The Moon is drawn from NASA's lunar color map, lit from the Sun's real direction and tilted as it appears from the park at its highest point that night. Moon imagery: NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio (CGI Moon Kit); LRO LROC and LOLA teams.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Solar timing uses NOAA approximations. Moonrise and moonset use a low-precision Meeus-style position. Checked against the U.S. Naval Observatory, they agree to within a few minutes: a minute or less at the parks checked in Alaska, Hawaiʻi, American Samoa and the Virgin Islands, and under 4 minutes at mid-latitude parks. Sunrise, sunset and twilight agree to within a minute. Moon illumination corrects the mean 29.53-day cycle with the Moon's calculated position and is approximate. Terrain and atmospheric conditions can shift visible rise and set times. The Moon is drawn from NASA's lunar color map, lit from the Sun's real direction and tilted as it appears from the park at its highest point that night. Moon imagery: NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio (CGI Moon Kit); LRO LROC and LOLA teams."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Los horarios solares usan aproximaciones de NOAA. La salida y la puesta de la Luna usan una posición de baja precisión al estilo de Meeus. Comparados con el U.S. Naval Observatory, coinciden con un margen de pocos minutos: un minuto o menos en los parques verificados de Alaska, Hawaiʻi, Samoa Americana y las Islas Vírgenes, y menos de 4 minutos en los parques de latitudes medias. La salida del sol, la puesta del sol y el crepúsculo coinciden con un margen de un minuto. La iluminación lunar corrige el ciclo medio de 29.53 días con la posición calculada de la Luna y es aproximada. El terreno y las condiciones atmosféricas pueden alterar las horas visibles de salida y puesta. La Luna se dibuja con el mapa de color lunar de la NASA, iluminada desde la dirección real del Sol e inclinada como se ve desde el parque en su punto más alto esa noche. Imágenes de la Luna: Scientific Visualization Studio de la NASA (CGI Moon Kit); equipos LRO LROC y LOLA."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Solid: forecast. Half-filled: an early look. Hollow: usual clouds. The ring marks the week's best night.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Solid: forecast. Half-filled: an early look. Hollow: usual clouds. The ring marks the week's best night."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Relleno: pronóstico. Medio relleno: vista anticipada. Sin relleno: nubosidad habitual. El anillo marca la mejor noche de la semana."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Solid: full forecast. Half-filled: an early look, the forecast eased toward the usual clouds. Hollow: no cloud forecast yet, so the park's usual clouds. Dot size follows the score; a cloud marks overcast skies. Past nights keep only a faint dot. A small streak marks a meteor shower's peak, a shaded Moon a lunar eclipse you can see; neither changes the score.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Solid: full forecast. Half-filled: an early look, the forecast eased toward the usual clouds. Hollow: no cloud forecast yet, so the park's usual clouds. Dot size follows the score; a cloud marks overcast skies. Past nights keep only a faint dot. A small streak marks a meteor shower's peak, a shaded Moon a lunar eclipse you can see; neither changes the score."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Relleno: pronóstico completo. Medio relleno: vista anticipada, el pronóstico ajustado hacia la nubosidad habitual. Sin relleno: aún sin pronóstico de nubes, así que cuenta la nubosidad habitual del parque. El tamaño del punto sigue al índice; una nube indica cielo cubierto. Las noches pasadas conservan solo un punto tenue. Un pequeño trazo marca el máximo de una lluvia de meteoros, y una Luna sombreada, un eclipse de Luna visible; ninguno cambia el índice."
          }
        }
      }
    },
