    "With headphones, a soft tone sits where the Milky Way's core, a planet or the Moon is, and quickens as you turn toward it, so you can find it with the screen dark. With AirPods that track your head, iOS asks once to use their motion; it stays on this iPhone. Nothing is recorded.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "device": {
              "ipad": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "With headphones, a soft tone sits where the Milky Way's core, a planet or the Moon is, and quickens as you turn toward it, so you can find it with the screen dark. With AirPods that track your head, iOS asks once to use their motion; it stays on this iPad. Nothing is recorded."
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "With headphones, a soft tone sits where the Milky Way's core, a planet or the Moon is, and quickens as you turn toward it, so you can find it with the screen dark. With AirPods that track your head, iOS asks once to use their motion; it stays on this iPhone. Nothing is recorded."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "variations": {
            "device": {
              "ipad": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "Con audífonos, un tono suave se ubica donde está el núcleo de la Vía Láctea, un planeta o la Luna, y se acelera al girar hacia él, para encontrarlo con la pantalla apagada. Con AirPods que siguen tu cabeza, iOS pide una vez usar su movimiento; se queda en este iPad. No se graba nada."
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "Con audífonos, un tono suave se ubica donde está el núcleo de la Vía Láctea, un planeta o la Luna, y se acelera al girar hacia él, para encontrarlo con la pantalla apagada. Con AirPods que siguen tu cabeza, iOS pide una vez usar su movimiento; se queda en este iPhone. No se graba nada."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
