    "iOS measures the average brightness of the pixels Nyx draws (MetricKit's average pixel luminance: 0% is an all-black screen, 100% all white) and reports it about once a day. It is measured on this iPhone and never leaves it.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "variations": {
            "device": {
              "ipad": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "iOS measures the average brightness of the pixels Nyx draws (MetricKit's average pixel luminance: 0% is an all-black screen, 100% all white) and reports it about once a day. It is measured on this iPad and never leaves it."
                }
              },
              "other": {
                "stringUnit": {
                  "state": "translated",
                  "value": "iOS measures the average brightness of the pixels Nyx draws (MetricKit's average pixel luminance: 0% is an all-black screen, 100% all white) and reports it about once a day. It is measured on this iPhone and never leaves it."
                }
